          "media_type": "application/json"
        }
      ],
      "claim": "A null material contrast establishes authorized structural inadequacy or suggests T3 execution in this activity.",
      "review": "A finite contrast cannot eliminate other authorized geometry/control values or establish a mechanism. This activity fixes T2 once selected; no T3 execution was authorized by a subsequent plan."
    },
    {
      "decisions": [
        {
          "artifact_id": "2e7714b4715dfb8bbb07b25c3972b9e95370c940102bcc93e3c7b1c6a3afe848",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        },
        {
          "artifact_id": "eba4ded02af94e3d21fb29c3608d594bbb45c033f868c1ab81a66b29af2805f8",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        }
      ],
      "claim": "Stiff improves speed by 9.5x against an identical-weight 0.8825765295566194 m/s baseline; compliant degrades every component.",
      "review": "The actual material runs use 0.05/0.1. Their identified historical T2 baseline speed is 1.1210197701767821 m/s, not the contemporary 0.025 baseline 0.8825765295566194. Stiff development speed is about 12.12x lower. Compliant worsens position and terminal error but improves speed to 0.13345246457739318; it is a trade-off, not worsening of all components. Material speed response is not monotone across compliant/baseline/stiff."
    },
    {
      "decisions": [
        {
          "artifact_id": "2e7714b4715dfb8bbb07b25c3972b9e95370c940102bcc93e3c7b1c6a3afe848",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        },
        {
          "artifact_id": "eba4ded02af94e3d21fb29c3608d594bbb45c033f868c1ab81a66b29af2805f8",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        }
      ],
      "claim": "The baseline holding error was stiffness-limited rather than a window-boundary artifact.",
      "review": "Changing numerical Young modulus changes the recorded closed-loop trajectory. This demonstrates sample-level sensitivity, but does not independently identify the physical or timing mechanism or eliminate a holding-window boundary explanation."
    },
    {
      "decisions": [
        {
          "artifact_id": "2e7714b4715dfb8bbb07b25c3972b9e95370c940102bcc93e3c7b1c6a3afe848",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        },
        {
          "artifact_id": "eba4ded02af94e3d21fb29c3608d594bbb45c033f868c1ab81a66b29af2805f8",
          "media_type": "application/json"
        }
      ],
      "claim": "Structural mutations require a contemporary source because historical T2 lacks semantic decisions.",
      "review": "The accepted material plan actually used historical v2-T2. The repaired failure was an inactive middle-parameter comparison on other two-segment historical templates. The finite-template projection derives semantic decisions from the fixed catalog and preserves historical source identity; contemporary-only sourcing is not established."
    },
    {
      "decisions": [
